# ADEPE — app environment
#
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) if you need to change anything. Nothing here
# is required: the defaults work for every local mode.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser. Never put a
# secret in this file — anything here ends up in the shipped JavaScript.


# Where Local proofs mode sends transactions to be proved. Defaults to the
# server `make proof-server` starts. Change it to prove on another machine.
# VITE_PROOF_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:6300


# The clinic's signing key, as 64 hex characters. Generate one with:
#   head -c 32 /dev/urandom | xxd -p -c 64
#
# Unset means a built-in demo key, so a fresh clone runs with no configuration.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TREATING IT AS A SECRET. Vite inlines every VITE_ variable
# into the bundle at build time, so this key ships to every visitor and anyone
# can extract it and mint credentials the contract accepts. Putting it here
# keeps it out of source control and lets a deployment use its own key. It does
# not make it private. The fix is a service that holds the key and returns
# signatures, which this project does not have.
#
# The deployed contract trusts exactly one issuer, so if you change this you
# must deploy again — `make deploy-preview` registers whichever key the app is
# built with. Preview mode compares the two and refuses to start if they
# disagree, rather than letting every application fail as "untrusted issuer".
# VITE_ISSUER_SEED=


# Preview testnet mode takes its indexer and proof server from the connected
# Lace wallet, and the contract address from ../deployment.preview.json, so
# there is nothing else to configure here.
